# Architecture

## Shape

- `backend/server.py` stays thin: FastAPI app, CORS, startup indexes, router mount.
- Domain logic lives in packages (`decision_engine/`, `life_graph/`, `knowledge/`, `documents/`, …).
- HTTP surface lives in `backend/routers/` and connector routers.
- Shared deps/auth/DB in `backend/deps.py`.
- Frontend routes in `frontend/app/` (expo-router). Shared UI/API in `frontend/src/`.

## API

- All HTTP APIs under `/api`.
- Health: `GET /api/` → `{ "app": "ORA", "status": "ok" }`.
- Auth: Bearer JWT from email/password or Google session bridge.

## Change rules

- Prefer extending an existing domain package over new top-level folders.
- Avoid cross-importing router files into other routers; go through services/deps.
- Feature flags via env vars (see existing `*_ENABLED` patterns).
- Keep Decision Engine / Life Graph / Knowledge boundaries intact unless the task explicitly requires crossing them.

## Naming

- Python: snake_case modules/functions, PascalCase classes.
- TS/TSX: camelCase values, PascalCase components, kebab-case route folders as already used.
- Collections: plural snake_case Mongo collections already in startup indexes.
